        "id": "download-msi-says-it-cannot-be-built-or-msiexec-fails-065",
        "text": "The is built by the server when it is downloaded. Add device shows the reason in words; the route answers with a code: Code Meaning What to do (503) The server publishes no signed agent, and only the signed agent takes a token on its command line. Use the or the command, or publish the signed agent (update signing.md). (503) or is missing on the server. on the portal host. No restart is needed. (503) Two packages are already being built. Try again in a moment. (400) The link was used, expired or was revoked (or the key is used up, expired or revoked). Make a new link or key. (400) The token in the URL is not 16–128 hexadecimal characters. Copy the link again. On the computer, writes a log ( is hidden in it). Exit code 1603 with \"Rem0te: pass TOKEN=…\" in the log is the launch condition: the package has no token, or the token has a space or a quote. Any other 1603 is the agent's install failing; its own log is , as for the . The has never been run on real Windows, so please report what you see. Uninstalling the from Programs and Features removes only its entry; the agent keeps running. To remove a computer, offboard it from the console."
