        "heading": "What has been proven, and what hasn't",
        "id": "what-has-been-proven-and-what-hasnt",
        "text": "Evidence Portal routes, scoping (business A / B, a Business User without access gets 404), containment, caps, receipts only from the agent, the long poll and its cap, user closed and inactivity endings, retention pruning, no message text in the audit log , the real API from on a scratch database, with the device simulated over the real device routes Text, names, support reasons, presence, receipts, retention bounds; the emoji lists, magic bytes, file names, download headers and caps (0.44) Files both ways, inline pictures against disguised files, headers, the 10 MB and per chat caps, scoping, containment, recording off, retention, the inbox and per user read marks, emoji through the text path (0.44) (port 3703), the real API from on a scratch database The tray host and the tray (0.36, replacing the 0.34 chat host): frames, hello nonce, the closed field set per frame, receipts, the unread badge, the per minute cap, the pipe server against a fake portal and a fake operating system; text cleaning and the limiter in Windows build and Static guarantees (routes, scoping, containment, secret, audit meta, caps, the window holding no secret, pipe flags and ACL) , the chat section The tray path (0.36): codes, the page, recording on and off, user started chats ; the page in Chromium by The window or the tray on a real Windows desktop, , the pipe DACL, session selection, Fast User Switching, RDP, WebView2, and (0.44) pictures, the file picker, paste, drop and downloads inside the WebView2 window None. Not run on Windows."
