        "id": "refusal-codes",
        "text": "Code Meaning Not a catalog action. Commands, scripts and the blocked categories are always this Requested through its own workflow, not the Actions tab: update install (a patch deployment) and, from 0.34, software install and uninstall (the software catalog) The parameters aren't the catalog's (another service, an extra field) Your role or access level doesn't include requesting this, on this computer The computer is a protected class No enrolled identity, a legacy agent, an agent that doesn't report the action, or a build other than the published one 0.32: the requested window is longer than the action allows (a restart schedule: 2 hours) An earlier request for this action on this computer is still unresolved An earlier outcome is uncertain. Reconcile it first Updates are requested through a patch deployment, and (0.34) script runs from the script library , , , 0.34 script runs: see Script library , , The signer didn't answer, or refused the plan (e.g. after a policy change, while the signer holds a pause, or for a script run ) 0.40 direct mode: confirm it is you (a fresh sign in) before a request that is signed at once 0.40: a ClientSt0r proposal for a business in direct mode. Only a person signed in to the portal can request one , 0.45: a service or process that is never changed from here (see What is protected). The computer refuses it again ( , ) , 0.45: the computer's latest service or process list doesn't show that service (with that display name) or that process (that id, name and start time). Refresh the tab , 0.45: the tab's reason: an agent without the action, offline, no signer, a pause, your access, or an earlier request on the computer still open Actions are paused for this business, or globally (Containment). An approved plan is held, not canceled, and is delivered when the pause is lifted Agent refusal reasons: , , , , , , , , , , , , , , , , (0.28: a signed covers this business or computer. Like every refusal it is final: lifting the pause doesn't revive the job; request it again), (from 0.32 also a restart plan whose window is over 2 hours). From 0.40 is also what an agent older than 0.40 answers to a direct mode plan, and what a 0.40 agent answers to a direct plan that asks for customer sign off. Signer codes added in 0.40: (a plan that says direct for a business in signed mode, or the other way), , and for a ring under a patch policy that was activated in direct mode after the business left it. 0.32 maintenance results that are not refusals: and (not executed, nothing changed), , , , , , , (an agent built without the maintenance surface). 0.34 software results: , and (refused, nothing installed), , and (not executed), , , , and (failed), (uncertain), (an agent built without the software surface). See Software deployment. 0.45 service and process results: , (another display name now), (a driver, or a boot or system start type), , (the process id now belongs to a process with another name or start time), , (all refused, nothing changed); and (nothing to do); , , , , and (failed); / (an agent built without them)."
