        "text": "Script library rem0te has a script library : PowerShell scripts that are written, versioned and reviewed in the portal. From 0.34, an approved version can be run on Windows computers, but only as a signed approved action ( ) after three separate approvals: the library review, two approvers adding the version's exact hash to the approval signer's own allowlist, and two approvers approving each run. Not yet run on a real Windows computer. The run path is tested end to end with the agent's real decision code and real PowerShell, but that is PowerShell 7 on Linux , not Windows PowerShell 5.1, through the simulator. The Windows job object, the SYSTEM context and Windows PowerShell's own behaviour haven't been run on a lab machine. See What has been proven."
