        "text": "The portal holds no key the agent accepts. The agent runs only plans signed by the approval signer's key, which it learns through the offline rooted update chain. A portal, or someone holding its database, can mark a library version Approved or write an ACTIVE allowlist row. That gets them rows in tables, not a signature: the signer decides from its own entry, and refuses ( ) a plan for an entry it doesn't hold. The portal can't write the allowlist. The signer's internal listener takes a proposal (always born awaiting approval ), answers status, and takes a revocation. It has no route that approves, activates or edits an entry; a proposal under an existing id with different content is refused ( ). The standard agent never executes. The heartbeat agent ( ) reports and reads. It only hands a delivered envelope and its content to the signed agent, which decides. There's no other route for it. The script library module creates no and reaches no dispatcher, signer or heartbeat. The only routes that touch running are the four of , and a run is requested nowhere else: with is . The security invariants (§14, §23, §39) check all of this in CI."
