        "text": "1. In Rem0te, add the provider with the client secret first (or none), then on its card under Trust and sign out choose Generate key . Rem0te creates a P 256 key; the private half is sealed in the database and never shown. 2. In Keycloak, Clients → rem0te → Credentials → Client Authenticator: Signed JWT , signature algorithm ES256 . 3. Keys tab: Use JWKS URL: On , and the JWKS URL Rem0te shows: . (Or switch it off and import the file from Download public JWKS .) 4. Back in Rem0te, set Token authentication to private key jwt . Sign in once to check, then remove the client secret from both sides. Replace key makes a new key with a new . With the JWKS URL, Keycloak picks it up on its next fetch; with an imported file, import the new one first."
