        "heading": "What a job can and cannot do",
        "id": "what-a-job-can-and-cannot-do",
        "text": "Can: read the ticket text ClientSt0r sent; read one computer's heartbeat freshness, agent version, OS build, uptime, memory and system disk headroom, pending updates and reboot required flag; call the inference gateway once per profile; return a signed result. Cannot: run a shell or any command, fetch any URL except the two in the peers file, open a remote session, issue a launcher token, queue an endpoint command, reveal a credential, or approve anything. (Proposing a catalog action, below, is a separate route, and it can't approve anything either.) The worker process does not load the modules that do those things, and fails CI if that changes. IP and MAC addresses, serial numbers, the logged on user and the domain are never sent to the gateway. A device reported computer name is reduced to a plain character set first. Tickets, Windows reported values and model output are all treated as untrusted: prompt injection patterns in the ticket are reported as ; a model \"fact\" whose evidence reference rem0te cannot resolve becomes an ; unknown fields in model output are dropped and counted; next steps are text ( ), and suggestions to extract credentials, disable defenses, delete backups, grant admin, wipe disks or run commands are labelled ; link hosts in draft replies are listed for the reviewer; a gateway response not signed for this exact request, job, organization and profile is rejected."
