        "id": "proposing-an-approved-action-026",
        "text": "ClientSt0r can propose a catalog action on one computer, today only with . The 0.32 maintenance actions (service restart, restart schedule and cancel, log collection) are not offered to ClientSt0r and a proposal naming one is : advertising them is a change to the ticket rmm contract that has not been agreed. It can't approve, dispatch or run one. The proposal goes through the same path as the portal's own Request approval button, as the delegated technician, and it gets the same live access check and the same approval signer. Route Delegation scope What it does Creates a plan awaiting approval, and returns its and Status, outcome and what the computer observed lists the proposable actions under . The list is empty until an approval signer is configured. No command field, ever. The request schema is strict: an names a catalog id and version, and must equal the catalog's. A , a , or a target given as a hostname is a schema error. An AI suggestion gets no shortcut. with a is shown to the approvers as such, and needs exactly the approvals a person's request needs. Idempotent. The same returns the same proposal; a different request under it is . Refusals pass through with the portal's codes: , , , , , , , and while actions are paused. Each is audited as with . The technician needs Request approved actions ( ) in that business, in addition to the mapping. Show to the people who will approve. Approval happens there, never in ClientSt0r. The whole lifecycle is described in approved actions.md."
